  "proven_findings": [
    "Both frozen 1835-row SFT completion corpora contain valid full JSON targets matching target objects exactly.",
    "Actual Qwen tokenizer leaves the final outer-closing token ]} supervised in every row in both corpora; zero final outer-closing tokens overlap UNKNOWN masks.",
    "SFT appends one supervised EOS after the complete target; no target contains internal EOS or padding tokens.",
    "All 29 invalid JSON outputs in six completed screen conditions swap their final two bracket characters: suffix }}] instead of }]}. Each JSON error is at the second-last character.",
    "A diagnostic swap of only the final two characters makes all 29 parse as JSON. This was not applied to prediction artifacts, gold or reported metrics.",
    "The existing stopping extractor rejects all 29 malformed outputs. Retokenized-prefix replay found no accepted earlier prefix. None reached max_new_tokens or had a runtime error.",
    "Stored generations omit raw generated IDs, EOS-observed flags and explicit stopping reason; EOS-versus-padding cannot be directly proved retrospectively."
  ],
  "interpretation": [
    "No demonstrated malformed-target, truncated-target, or terminal-closure loss-mask defect in the frozen data and training path.",
    "The observed failure is malformed outer closure generation after fine-tuning, rather than merely an unfinished valid JSON prefix.",
    "Insufficient optimization, changes to grammar probabilities during partial SFT, and exposure to masked placeholder context remain plausible but unproved causes.",
    "The decoder can terminate on model EOS independently of valid JSON. Premature EOS remains plausible, but cannot be established from stripped decoded strings alone.",
    "The stopping extractor permits wrapped/first-object JSON while scoring uses strict whole-string JSON; this general contract mismatch is real, but was not responsible for accepting the 29 observed malformed endings."
  ],
  "recommendations": [
    "Preserve current frozen results and report structural-invalid rate separately from semantic precision/recall.",
    "In a new versioned diagnostic runner, record generated token IDs, EOS/pad IDs, first-JSON-complete event, actual stop reason and unstripped final tokens.",
    "Replay a small fixed set of affected prompts with the same checkpoint to distinguish model EOS from padding removal; do not alter the ongoing GPU queue.",
    "After the baseline is frozen, compare grammar-constrained decoding or a separately trained structure objective. Keep raw and constrained metrics separate; do not silently repair existing outputs.",
    "Do not unmask UNKNOWN empty decisions to teach syntax, because that would incorrectly convert unannotated pairs into negatives."
